{"created": "2020-09-07T14:01:05.168151+00:00", "modified": "2020-09-28T08:20:21.562365+00:00", "id": 4017659, "conceptrecid": "4017658", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.4017659", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.4017658", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4017659", "metadata": {"title": "Dataset of BattLeDIM: Battle of the Leakage Detection and Isolation Methods", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.4017659", "publication_date": "2020-09-07", "description": "<p>Drinking Water Distribution Networks (DWDN) are susceptible to infrastructure failures, which may lead to water losses. Typically, these water losses are due to background leakages and pipe bursts which may occur anywhere within the distribution network. Background leakages are normally difficult to detect due to their small size, whereas pipe bursts are easier to locate as they are of larger size and may appear on the surface. The early detection and localization of some leakage event is extremely important, as this would reduce the time required for accommodating the event and therefore reducing the risk of further infrastructure degradation, contamination events and consumer complaints.</p>\n\n<p>In previous years, a number of methodologies have been proposed to detect and isolate the location of leakage events using various types of sensor measurements. These methods were commonly evaluated on private commercial datasets, and as a result, it is not possible to objectively compare these methods in their ability to detect and isolate leaks. In the past year, a leakage detection dataset has been proposed, LeakDB, based on benchmark networks and created using the WNTR tool, using pressure-driven demands and realistic leakage modelling. Inspired by the &ldquo;BATtle of the Attack Detection ALgorithms&rdquo; (BATADAL), which focused on the detection of cyber-physical attacks, our team decided to organize a similar &ldquo;battle&rdquo; focusing on leakage events.</p>\n\n<p>The Battle of the Leakage Detection and Isolation Methods (BattLeDIM),&nbsp; aims at objectively comparing the performance of methods for the detection and localization of leakage events, relying on SCADA measurements of flow and pressure sensors installed within water distribution networks. Participants may use different types of tools and methods, including (but not limited to) engineering judgement, machine learning, statistical methods, signal processing, and model-based fault diagnosis approaches.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Stelios G. Vrachimis", "affiliation": "KIOS Research and Innovation Center of Excellence", "orcid": "0000-0001-8862-5205"}, {"name": "Demetrios G. Eliades", "affiliation": "KIOS Research and Innovation Center of Excellence", "orcid": "0000-0001-6184-6366"}, {"name": "Riccardo Taormina", "affiliation": "Delft University of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0002-1550-504X"}, {"name": "Avi Ostfeld", "affiliation": "Technion \u2013 Israel Institute of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0001-9112-6079"}, {"name": "Zoran Kapelan", "affiliation": "Delft University of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0002-0934-4470"}, {"name": "Shuming Liu", "affiliation": "Tsinghua University", "orcid": "0000-0002-0977-565X"}, {"name": "Marios S. Kyriakou", "affiliation": "KIOS Research and Innovation Center of Excellence", "orcid": "0000-0002-2324-8661"}, {"name": "Pavlos Pavlou", "affiliation": "KIOS Research and Innovation Center of Excellence"}, {"name": "Mengning Qiu", "affiliation": "Technion \u2013 Israel Institute of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0001-8971-2570"}, {"name": "Marios Polycarpou", "affiliation": "KIOS Research and Innovation Center of Excellence", "orcid": "0000-0001-6495-9171"}], "keywords": ["battledim, battledim 2020, water distribution, networks, leakage detection, leakage localization, fault diagnosis, benchmark"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.3902046", "relation": "isDocumentedBy", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "http://battledim.ucy.ac.cy/", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/KIOS-Research/BattLeDIM", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "scheme": "url"}], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "grants": [{"code": "739551", "internal_id": "10.13039/501100000780::739551", "funder": {"name": "European Commission", "doi": "10.13039/501100000780", "acronym": "EC"}, "title": "KIOS Research and Innovation Centre of Excellence", "acronym": "KIOS CoE", "program": "H2020-EU.4.a.", "url": "https://cordis.europa.eu/projects/739551"}], "communities": [{"id": "eu"}, {"id": "battledim2020"}, {"id": "kios-coe"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "4017658"}}]}}, "title": "Dataset of BattLeDIM: Battle of the Leakage Detection and Isolation Methods", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4017659", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/4017659", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/4017659?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4017659", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4017659", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.4017659", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4017659/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4017658", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/4017658", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4017658", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.4017658", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:4017659/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:4017659/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4017659/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4017659/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4017659/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4017659/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/401765